first_claim:
An apparatus comprising:
 means for detecting an audio signal; 
 means for determining a first score for the audio signal, wherein the first score indicates an authenticity of the audio signal; 
 means for embedding the first score in an audio output; and 
 means for providing the audio output.

all_claims:
An apparatus comprising:
 means for detecting an audio signal; 
 means for determining a first score for the audio signal, wherein the first score indicates an authenticity of the audio signal; 
 means for embedding the first score in an audio output; and 
 means for providing the audio output.

An apparatus as claimed in any one of the preceding claims, further comprising:
 means for determining a direction of arrival of the audio signal; 
 means for determining whether there is presence of a human in the direction of arrival of the audio signal; 
 wherein the first score indicates that the authenticity of the audio signal is above the first threshold if the presence of a human in the direction of arrival of the audio signal is determined.

A system comprising a first detection device and a user device, wherein:
 the first detection device is configured to:
 detect an audio signal; 
 determine a first score for the audio signal, wherein the first score indicates an authenticity of the audio signal; 
 embed the first score in an audio output; and 
 provide the audio output; and 
 the user device is configured to:
 receive the audio output from the first detection device; 
 extract the first score from the audio output; and 
 determine whether to perform one or more actions in response to one or more commands based, at least in part, on the first score.

A method comprising:
 detecting an audio signal; 
 determining a first score for the audio signal, wherein the first score indicates an authenticity of the audio signal; 
 embedding the first score in an audio output; and 
 providing the audio output.

A computer program comprising instructions for causing an apparatus to perform at least the following:
 detecting an audio signal; 
 determining a first score for the audio signal, wherein the first score indicates an authenticity of the audio signal; 
 embedding the first score in an audio output; and 
 providing the audio output.
